From 7c185e7ea43fb8382a81062526f2d884ad789eb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Assaf Berg <asssaf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 18:57:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Support optional reboot parameter via direct syscall and
 /run/reboot-param (#1)

* reboot: support optional reboot parameter with direct syscall and file-passing for graceful shutdown

This commit updates the reboot applet and init process to support passing a second parameter (e.g. "2" or "0 tryboot") to the reboot syscall.

1. Added necessary Linux reboot syscall constants and magic numbers to init/reboot.h.
2. In init/halt.c, parsed any optional arguments provided to 'reboot'. If forcing with '-f', we call syscall(SYS_reboot, ...) with LINUX_REBOOT_CMD_RESTART2 directly to bypass the libc wrapper. If not forcing, we write the parameter to '/run/reboot-param' and notify init.
3. In init/init.c, during low-level reboot, we check if '/run/reboot-param' exists. If so, we read it, delete it, and call the syscall using LINUX_REBOOT_CMD_RESTART2 with the parameter.
4. Added REBOOT_PARAM to usage instructions in init/halt.c.

Co-authored-by: asssaf <445552+asssaf@users.noreply.github.com>

* reboot: update optional parameter handling with REBOOT_PARAM_FILE macro and safer file handling

- Used the REBOOT_PARAM_FILE macro for "/run/reboot-param" defined in reboot.h.
- Configured the file creation permissions to be 0600 instead of 0666.
- Ensured that the unlink of the file always happens when the file was successfully opened, even if read errors or an empty file occur.

Co-authored-by: asssaf <445552+asssaf@users.noreply.github.com>

